.TH "LAM" "1" "June 2026" "Lambë 0.12.0" ""
.SH AUTHOR
Hakim Jonas Ghoula
.SH NAME
.PP
lam - query structured data files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBlam\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIEXPRESSION\fR [\fIFILE\fR]
.PP
\fBlam\fR \fB-i\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Query JSON, YAML, TOML, HCL, CSV, TSV, and Markdown files using a composable pipeline DSL. Format is auto-detected from file extension.
.PP
Lambë infers the structural shape of query results and reports incompatibilities with target output formats. Use \fB--explain\fR to trace the shape at each pipeline stage, or the \fBas\fR(\fIfmt\fR) combinator inside a query to bridge common mismatches.
.PP
If no file is given, reads from standard input.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB-p\fR, \fB--pretty\fR
Pretty-print output. On by default.
.TP
\fB--no-pretty\fR
Disable pretty-printing.
.TP
\fB-r\fR, \fB--raw\fR
Output top-level string scalars without quotes. No effect on structured output (objects, arrays, numbers, booleans, null) — those still serialize through the active output format.
.TP
\fB-f\fR, \fB--format\fR \fIFMT\fR
Input format. One of: json, yaml, toml, hcl, csv, tsv, markdown. Auto-detected from file extension if omitted.
.TP
\fB-t\fR, \fB--to\fR \fIFMT\fR
Output format. One of: json, yaml, toml, csv, tsv, hcl. Default is json.
.TP
\fB--flatten-cells\fR \fIPOLICY\fR
CSV/TSV policy for non-scalar cells. \fBrefuse\fR (default) rejects list- or map-valued cells with a shape error. \fBjson\fR encodes them as JSON strings inline; the shape check correspondingly widens to accept any list at the root. Ignored for other output formats.
.TP
\fB--schema\fR \fIPATH\fR
Path to a JSON Schema subset file. Threads the declared shape through inference and \fB--explain\fR, validates data against the schema at load time (errors on concrete-type disagreement), and fills in shape details the sampled data doesn't cover (empty-list elements, optional fields). Auto-detected as a sibling \fB.schema.json\fR if omitted. Accepts \fBtype\fR, \fBproperties\fR, \fBitems\fR, and \fBrequired\fR; rejects structural combinators (allOf/oneOf/$ref) and value-level constraints (minimum/pattern/enum/etc) with a per-keyword error.
.TP
\fB--print-shape\fR
Print the inferred shape of the data as a JSON Schema subset document. Replaces the 0.8.0 \fB--schema\fR flag with the same meaning, renamed because \fB--schema\fR now takes a path value.
.TP
\fB--explain\fR
Trace the shape of values flowing through each pipeline stage. Static analysis only; does not execute the query. Reports which output formats the final shape can be serialized as. Flags provably-empty filters and runtime-rejection mismatches.
.TP
\fB--explain-trivial\fR
Include trivial-result warnings in the explain report. Flags parameterised ops (\fBsort_by\fR, \fBgroup_by\fR, \fBmap\fR, \fBunique_by\fR) whose argument references a field provably absent on the element shape. Implies \fB--explain\fR.
.TP
\fB--explain-json\fR
Emit the explain report as a JSON document instead of the text table. Useful for agent tooling or build-pipeline integration. Implies \fB--explain\fR.
.TP
\fB--assert\fR
Evaluate the expression and exit with code 0 if the result is true, 1 if false.
.TP
\fB-i\fR, \fB--interactive\fR
Start the interactive REPL. Requires a file argument.
.TP
\fB--ndjson\fR
Treat input as ndjson or jsonl: one JSON document per line, evaluated independently with no state shared between lines. Emits one compact JSON result per line on stdout. Auto-enabled when the file extension is \fB.ndjson\fR or \fB.jsonl\fR. Cannot combine with \fB--interactive\fR, \fB--schema\fR, \fB--print-shape\fR, \fB--assert\fR, or \fB--explain\fR. Output must be JSON (\fB--to json\fR or default); other \fB--to\fR values are refused.
.TP
\fB-n\fR, \fB--null-input\fR
Run the query against \fBnull\fR context with no input. Useful for value computations like \fClam -n '[1,2,3] | unique'\fR. Without \fB-n\fR, the missing-input guard fires (a typo'd filename or missing redirect is a common footgun); the flag makes the "I have no input" intent explicit. Cannot combine with \fB--interactive\fR, \fB--ndjson\fR, \fB--schema\fR, or \fB--assert\fR.
.TP
\fB--skill\fR
Print the embedded agent SKILL.md to stdout and exit. Lets agent harnesses install the skill regardless of how \fClam\fR was acquired: \fClam --skill > .agents/skills/lambe/SKILL.md\fR. The content is captured at compile time from \fC.agents/skills/lambe/SKILL.md\fR in the lambë source.
.TP
\fB-h\fR, \fB--help\fR
Show usage information.
.SH QUERY LANGUAGE
.PP
Queries start with \fB.\fR (the current document) and chain operations with \fB|\fR.
.SS Field access
.PP
\fB.name\fR accesses a field. \fB.a.b.c\fR chains access. Missing fields return null.
.SS Indexing
.PP
\fB.[0]\fR indexes into a list. \fB.[-1]\fR indexes from the end. Out of bounds returns null.
.SS Slicing
.PP
\fB.[1:3]\fR extracts elements 1 and 2. \fB.[:3]\fR from the start. \fB.[2:]\fR to the end. \fB.[:-1]\fR all except the last.
.SS Arithmetic
.PP
+, -, *, /, % on numbers.
.SS Comparison
.PP
<, >, <=, >= on numbers. ==, != on any type.
.SS Boolean logic
.PP
&&, ||, ! with short-circuit evaluation.
.SS String interpolation
.PP
\fB"\\(.name) is \\(.age)"\fR evaluates expressions inside strings.
.SS Object construction
.PP
{name, total: .price * .qty} constructs a new object. {name} expands to {name: .name}.
.SS Conditionals
.PP
\fBif\fR \fIcond\fR \fBthen\fR \fIa\fR \fBelse\fR \fIb\fR
.SS Pipelines
.PP
\fB|\fR passes the left result into the right operation. Pipelines bind tighter than binary operators.
.SH PIPELINE OPERATIONS
.TP
\fBfilter\fR(\fIpred\fR)
Keep elements where \fIpred\fR is true.
.TP
\fBmap\fR(\fIexpr\fR)
Transform each element.
.TP
\fBsort\fR
Sort by natural order.
.TP
\fBsort_by\fR(\fIkey\fR)
Sort by a key expression.
.TP
\fBgroup_by\fR(\fIkey\fR)
Group into [{key, values}].
.TP
\fBunique\fR
Remove duplicates.
.TP
\fBunique_by\fR(\fIkey\fR)
Remove duplicates by key.
.TP
\fBflatten\fR
Flatten one level.
.TP
\fBreverse\fR
Reverse order.
.TP
\fBkeys\fR
Map keys or list indices.
.TP
\fBvalues\fR
Map values.
.TP
\fBlength\fR
Length of list, map, or string.
.TP
\fBfirst\fR, \fBlast\fR
First or last element.
.TP
\fBsum\fR (jq alias: \fBadd\fR), \fBavg\fR, \fBmin\fR, \fBmax\fR
Aggregate operations on numeric lists. \fCadd\fR is accepted for jq-compatibility; \fC--explain\fR canonicalises to \fCsum\fR.
.TP
\fBhas\fR(\fIkey\fR)
Check if a map contains a key.
.TP
\fBto_entries\fR
Map to [{key, value}].
.TP
\fBfrom_entries\fR
[{key, value}] to map.
.TP
\fBto_number\fR (jq alias: \fBtonumber\fR)
Parse a string as a number. Pass-through for existing numbers. Both names parse identically; \fC--explain\fR canonicalises to \fCto_number\fR.
.TP
\fBtype\fR
Runtime type of the value as a string: "null", "boolean", "number", "string", "array", or "object".
.TP
\fBfilter_values\fR(\fIpred\fR)
Filter a map's values.
.TP
\fBmap_values\fR(\fIexpr\fR)
Transform a map's values.
.TP
\fBfilter_keys\fR(\fIpred\fR)
Filter a map's keys.
.TP
\fBas\fR(\fIfmt\fR)
Shape-directed bridge to an output format. No-op when the current shape already satisfies \fIfmt\fR. Applies a single curated bridge when one exists. Errors with a list of candidates when more than one could apply. Valid \fIfmt\fR: json, yaml, toml, csv, tsv, hcl.
.SH NULL PROPAGATION
.PP
Navigation on null returns null: \fB.missing\fR returns null, \fB.missing.nested\fR returns null.
.PP
Computation on null throws: \fBnull + 5\fR and \fBnull > 3\fR are errors.
.SH INTERACTIVE MODE
.PP
\fBlam -i\fR \fIfile\fR starts the REPL. Type queries at the \fBlambe>\fR prompt. REPL commands start with \fB:\fR to distinguish them from queries.
.TP
\fB:schema\fR
Show data structure.
.TP
\fB:to\fR \fIfmt\fR
Set output format.
.TP
\fB:raw\fR
Toggle unquoted string output.
.TP
\fB:pretty\fR
Toggle pretty-printing.
.TP
\fB:flatten-cells\fR \fIPOLICY\fR
Set CSV/TSV cell policy for this session. One of: refuse, json.
.TP
\fB:load\fR \fIfile\fR
Load a different data file.
.TP
\fB:history\fR
Show query history.
.TP
\fB:help\fR
Show available commands.
.TP
\fB:quit\fR, \fB:q\fR
Exit.
.PP
Tab completes field names and pipeline operations. Up/Down navigates history. Ctrl+R searches history.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fR
Success, or \fB--assert\fR passed.
.TP
\fB1\fR
Error, or \fB--assert\fR failed.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB~/.lambe_history\fR
REPL command history, persisted between sessions.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Extract a value:
.PP
.nf
lam '.database.host' config.toml
.fi
.PP
Filter and project:
.PP
.nf
lam '.users | filter(.age > 30) | map(.name)' data.json
.fi
.PP
Aggregate:
.PP
.nf
lam '.items | map(.price) | sum' data.json
.fi
.PP
Format conversion:
.PP
.nf
lam --to yaml '.config' data.json
.fi
.PP
Shape inspection:
.PP
.nf
lam --print-shape deployment.yaml
.fi
.PP
Schema-checked query (validates data against the schema before running):
.PP
.nf
lam --schema api.schema.json '.users | map(.email)' response.json
.fi
.PP
Shape trace, schema-seeded (no data needed):
.PP
.nf
lam --schema api.schema.json --explain '.users | map(.email)'
.fi
.PP
Shape trace for a pipeline:
.PP
.nf
lam --explain '.users | filter(.age > 30) | map(.name)' data.json
.fi
.PP
Bridge to an output format inside the query:
.PP
.nf
lam --to toml '.dependencies | as(toml)' pubspec.yaml
.fi
.PP
CI validation:
.PP
.nf
lam --assert '.version != "0.0.0"' package.json
.fi
.PP
Pipe from stdin:
.PP
.nf
curl -s https://api.example.com/data | lam '.results | first'
.fi
.PP
Interactive exploration:
.PP
.nf
lam -i data.json
.fi
.PP
Line-delimited JSON (logs, event streams):
.PP
.nf
lam --ndjson '.level' events.ndjson
tail -f app.log | lam --ndjson '.user.id'
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBjq\fR(1) — the established JSON query tool. Lambë shares its pipeline aesthetic and extends to multi-format input with shape-aware output.
.SH BUGS
.PP
Report issues at https://github.com/hakimjonas/lambe/issues.
